menu "Station: receiver package staging"

    config PKG_STORE_RAM
        bool "Stage receiver packages in PSRAM on a board without the package partition"
        default y
        help
            A board whose partition table has no "gnss_pkg" partition (8 MB
            flash) keeps the package in one PSRAM buffer instead, from the
            download or upload to the end of the receiver update. It is not
            kept over a restart: an update cut short by one is finished
            with the same package downloaded (or uploaded) again. Off: no
            receiver updates on such a board.

    config PKG_STORE_RAM_MAX_KB
        int "Largest package staged in PSRAM (KB)"
        depends on PKG_STORE_RAM
        range 1024 6144
        default 3584
        help
            The largest receiver package is about 3 MB (UM980 build 25735:
            3,024,000 bytes; UM982 build 23575: 3,043,556 bytes).

    config PKG_STORE_RAM_MARGIN_KB
        int "PSRAM kept free beside a staged package (KB)"
        depends on PKG_STORE_RAM
        range 256 4096
        default 1024
        help
            A package is staged only when PSRAM has one free block of its
            size plus this much more: the flasher's decompression buffer
            (256 KB) and everything else the station allocates meanwhile.

endmenu
